### Remaining Concerns
- **Your call: how the Discipline section ends.** It used to close on Price's "no off switch" pull-quote; it now closes on Christopher's unresolved challenge to the mother story. I think that gives the skeptic's case its weight and sets up 1992 better, but it is a different closing note. Reverting means moving one block back.
- **Length is 64 words under the lint ceiling.** The bridges cost 57 words. Any later stage that adds copy will fail lint unless something is cut first; the ledger's own cut candidates are still the place to look.
- **Sean Penn appears once and never again.** That "chapters the highlight reel skips" paragraph reads like a coverage list, and only the Rocco custody fight pays off. Cutting the Penn clause would tighten it.
- **Small overstatement in the closing argument.** "She spent the speech on the person who told her she was finished" comes right after a quote from the part of the speech where she "turned serious." I left the wording alone.
- **Stale ledger pointer.** The fingerprint ledger's "Interior beat" line still names the old H2, "What Nearly Dying Changed About Madonna." I did not edit ledgers.
